  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Public Health through Surveillance, Epidemiologic Research, Disease Detection and Prevention: Conducting Public Health Research in Thailand; Technical Collaboration with the Ministry of Public Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) global health efforts are to assist Ministries of Health and other international partners to plan, effectively manage and conduct public health research in the intent of public health protection; achieve US Government program and international organization goals to improve health; including surveillance, intervention and prevention in global health programs that focus on leading causes of global health security, mortality, morbidity and disability including infectious diseases including bacterial, viral and parasitic diseases , non-communicable diseases, injury and violence, environmental health, generate and apply new knowledge to achieve public health goals and strengthen public health systems and capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
